 .. _`abbreviation codes`: https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0425/#python-tag
 .. _`compressed tag set`: https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0425/#compressed-tag-sets
 .. _`platform compatibility tags`: https://packaging.python.org/specifications/platform-compatibility-tags/
+
+
+Stateful compatibility selection
+-------------------------------
+
+``create_compatible_tags_selector(supported_tags)`` returns a callable
+``CompatibleTagsSelector``. Neither creating it nor calling it consumes inputs.
+On first advance, each query snapshots its finite candidate iterable and tag
+memberships, retaining payload identities. Entries are ordered by the first
+matching supported tag, with input order breaking ties. Duplicate payloads
+remain distinct entries. The supported source's preference order is authoritative:
+on Linux, compatible manylinux tags precede the corresponding plain linux tags.
+
+``selector(candidates, limit=None)`` accepts a nonnegative integer or None.
+Invalid limits raise at call time; zero does not touch either input.
+Iteration stops as soon as the limit or all matches are satisfied.
+
+Queries have independent cursors over one shared lazy cache. A suspended query
+sees tags added by other queries. Closing a query leaves the source available.
+This supports single-threaded interleaving, not concurrent threads.
+
+``cached_tags`` is a read-only tuple snapshot of distinct consumed supported tags.
+``exhausted`` becomes true only upon observing normal StopIteration. Cached tags
+remain useful after exhaustion, and the source is not polled again.
+An ordinary source exception is remembered at the cache boundary: later queries
+replay cached tags, and only queries needing more tags receive its type and
+message. No retry occurs. Empty and zero-limit queries do not surface it.
+Candidate input failures are local to their query.
